{"ld": 1750, "paper": "HP1168", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Require the Attorney General to Create and Update Biennially a Model Residential Lease", "sponsor_id": "h-boyer-david", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-arata-amy", "h-caruso-elizabeth", "h-foley-robert", "h-henderson-rachel", "h-kuhn-amy", "h-lee-adam", "h-montell-karen", "h-poirier-jennifer", "s-talbot-ross-rachel"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "This bill requires the Attorney General to create and post on its publicly accessible website a model residential lease that complies with current law, including any disclosure and any document required to be attached to a residential lease, and to update the model lease biennially. The bill requires the Attorney General to consult with one or more tenant advocacy organizations and one or more landlord advocacy organizations in creating and revising the model lease. It requires that the model lease be neutral and not favor either tenant or landlord rights and interests and requires posting for public comment a draft of the model lease on a publicly accessible website for 30 days prior to posting the final version.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1168&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2025-06-25", "governor_action": "Unsigned", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-25"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1750)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1168&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-601)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1168&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-601)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=